+## Summary
+
+Implement `build_reminder` as a single pure Python function. It will gate on strict confirmation, validate required action fields only once confirmed, parse a zero-offset ISO-8601 timestamp, choose the normal or fallback reminder instant, and produce canonical `Z` timestamps without changing the input mapping.
+
+## Technical Approach
+
+Use only Python's standard `datetime` module. Treat `confirmed is True` as the eligibility gate, so values such as `1` never create a reminder. Parse `Z` by converting it to `+00:00` for `datetime.fromisoformat`, then require a zero UTC offset and serialize every output timestamp with `Z`. Compare the parsed due time to the supplied aware `now`; return `None` for elapsed actions; use the 24-hour candidate unless it is before now, then use `now + 5 minutes` only if it is strictly before the due time.
+
+## Architecture
+
+No new architecture is warranted. The existing single module remains the only production surface; small private helpers keep validation, parsing, and formatting readable without adding a dependency or service boundary.
